#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fold_while

#% text
# `fold_while(f, x, xs, test)` folds like `fold(f, x, xs)` while `test` of the latest value gives `true`, and gives the first value for which it does not (or the last value, when the list ends). `fold_while(f, x, xs, test, m)` applies `test` to the latest `m` values, and `fold_while(f, x, xs, test, m, k)` gives the value `k` places before that one (`k <= 0`).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fold_while((a, b) => a/b, 120, range(10), is_integer)
#% output
#= 1/6

#% cell
fold_while((a, b) => a/b, 120, range(10), is_integer, 1, -1)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
fold_while((a, b) => a - b, 12, range(6), is_positive)
#% output
#= -3

